  "question": {
    "text": "If a curve <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and satisfies the differential equation, <math><mi>y</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to",
